type: software
title: "SIR: Synergy via Isotonic Regression"
abbreviation: "SIR"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-09"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20604671
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20604671"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AsiaeeLab/isosynergy"
keywords:
  - drug combinations
  - drug synergy
  - isotonic regression
  - wild bootstrap
  - shape-constrained regression
  - hypothesis testing
  - R package
abstract: >
  SIR (Synergy via Isotonic Regression) is a nonparametric R package for
  drug-combination synergy testing. It defines interaction as the deviation from
  a monotone-additive null fit by 2D isotonic regression and returns a
  calibrated per-matrix p-value via a degrees-of-freedom-corrected wild
  bootstrap, together with the interaction surface and effect size. Reference
  implementations of the Bliss, HSA, Loewe, and ZIP baselines are included for
  comparison.
